# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Alice E. A. Allen et al. (2024). Learning together: Towards foundation models for machine learning interatomic potentials with meta-learning.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-024-01339-x  arXiv:2307.04012v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2307.04012v1 (sha256 e195f3787adfb6fe...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 255 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/allen2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: ANI potentials (ANI-1x architecture in TorchANI)
# pre-trained with the Reptile meta-learning algorithm or by joint fitting
# (k = 1) on data sets computed at different levels of theory and refitted
# to a new level of theory: the aspirin MP2 test (Sec. III A), the
# CCSD(T) ANI-1ccx refits after pre-training on ANI-1x or on the six-data-
# set organic pre-training set (Sec. III C), and the CCSD(T) errors after
# pre-training on single data sets (Table S1). The QM9 study (Fig. 4) and
# the 3BPA learning curves, torsion scans and bond dissociation (Figs. 6,
# 7, S4-S8) are figure-only and not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-allen2024 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Allen et al. (2024): meta-learning (Reptile) to pre-train ANI potentials on data sets with different levels of theory" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-allen2024 .

entity:article-allen2024 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:sameAs <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41524-024-01339-x> ;
    schema:datePublished "2024"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:name "Learning together: Towards foundation models for machine learning interatomic potentials with meta-learning" ;
