###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The meta-learning (Reptile) refit errors of the aspirin study (minimum near k = 400), of the QM9 study and of 3BPA are shown only in figures. The k = 1 ANI-1x pre-training error for the CCSD(T) task is stated as 3.30 +/- 0.10 kcal/mol in the text and 3.47 kcal/mol in the Fig. 5 caption, so that model is not encoded; the k used for the meta-learned ANI-1x model is not stated in the text (k = 50 in the Fig. 5 caption).
# - The CCSD(T) errors are taken to be energy RMSEs in kcal/mol (Sec. III C states RMSEs; Table S1 says 'CCSD(T) error' and its no-pre-training value matches the 13.90 kcal/mol RMSE of Fig. S2). The split of the Sec. III C errors is not stated, so they have no role.
# - ANI hyperparameters are those of ANI-1x (Ref. [31]) and are not restated; the Reptile parameters k, epsilon and the 150-epoch refit limit have no hyperparameter individual. Batch size 250 and the learning-rate schedule (0.001 halved on plateau down to 1e-5) of SI S1.2/S1.5 are not tied to a specific model.
# - QMugs, GEOM, QM7-x and Transition-1x enter only through the combined pre-training set; QMugs and GEOM provide energies only (SI S1.2). QM9 (228 levels of theory) is used only in the figure-only study and is not encoded as a data set.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/allen2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

